---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/github';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How DIC works"
  description="Digital image correlation in five minutes — for Semper users."
  path="/learn/dic"
>
  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 3rem">
    <p class="crumb">
      <a href={withBase('/')}>← Home</a>
    </p>
    <h2>How DIC works</h2>
    <p class="sub">Enough theory to use Semper and read the Manual.</p>

    <div class="prose">
      <ol>
        <li>A specimen is painted with a random <strong>speckle pattern</strong>.</li>
        <li>A <strong>reference</strong> photo is taken, then more photos while it deforms.</li>
        <li>
          The image is divided into small windows called <strong>subsets</strong> (odd widths,
          indexed around the centre pixel).
        </li>
        <li>
          For each subset the engine finds where it moved in the deformed image, to about 1/100th of
          a pixel, using <strong>ICGN</strong> and <strong>ZNSSD</strong> (a difference score immune
          to lighting changes; lower is better).
        </li>
        <li>
          Displacements (<strong>U</strong>, <strong>V</strong> in pixels) are differentiated into
          strains (<strong>Exx</strong>, <strong>Eyy</strong>, <strong>Exy</strong> in millistrain).
        </li>
      </ol>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Field</th>
            <th>Meaning</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>U, V</td>
            <td>Horizontal / vertical displacement (px)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Exx, Eyy, Exy</td>
            <td>Normal and shear strain (mε)</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <div class="callout">
        Semper runs this pipeline on the phone. There is no scale calibration — convert pixels to
        physical units yourself. For experiment design, see the
        <a href="https://idics.org/guide/" rel="noopener noreferrer">iDICs Good Practices Guide</a>.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="cta-row" style="margin-top: 1.5rem">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href={withBase('/manual')}>Manual</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={withBase('/learn/glossary')}>Glossary</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
